G2908.b:
⟪κρείσσων⟫
(Epic and old Att.) and κρείττων (later Att.), prop. comparat. of κρατύς, strong, but in sense often (as in cl., v. LS, s.v.) as comparat. of ἀγαθός, [in LXX chiefly for ⁨טוֹב⁩;] ⟪better⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ as to advantage or usefulness: ⟦1 Corinthians 11:17|I Co 11:17⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:40|He 11:40⟧ ⟦Hebrews 12:24|12:24⟧; πολλῷ μᾶλλον κ., ⟦Philippians 1:23|Phl 1:23⟧; κρεῖσσον ποιεῖν, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:38|I Co 7:38⟧; ἐστιν, seq. inf., ⟦1 Corinthians 7:9|I Co 7:9⟧, ⟦2 Peter 2:21|II Pe 2:21⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ as to excellence: ⟦Hebrews 1:4|He 1:4⟧ ⟦Hebrews 6:9|6:9⟧ ⟦Hebrews 7:7|7:7⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:19|19⟧, ⟦Hebrews 7:22|22⟧ ⟦Hebrews 8:6|8:6⟧ ⟦Hebrews 9:23|9:23⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:34|10:34⟧ ⟦Hebrews 11:16|11:16⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:35|35⟧; κ. ἐστι, seq. inf., ⟦1 Peter 3:17|I Pe 3:17⟧.†

